{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791047514,"nonce":"sOwlbFgREpiarjQCDFdQbwlXp8A=","title":"Backdrop filters: Tailwind's backdrop-blur-* and backdrop colour filters","message":"CSS backdrop-filter blurs and colour-filters what is already drawn behind an element's box before the element draws over it. Tw refuses backdrop- classes until it is drawn.\n\nRenderer side done (see the commit citing this issue): DisplayList.PRIM_BACKDROP records; for each, the renderer blurs the target's rows under the element's box (grown by three deviations) into the target's second texture with BackdropRowsShader, then resumes the target and draws BackdropShader over the box, blurring down the columns, applying the colour matrix and covering the element's rounded box under its clips. A frame holding a backdrop is drawn into an offscreen frame layer and copied to the target by BlitShader, since a window surface cannot be read back.\n\nWaiting on Blinc: RenderProps has no backdrop filter (only filter, layer_effects and the Glass brush), and ashui's reactive props write only RenderProps. Asked blinc-b1 for RenderProps.backdrop_filter: Option\u003cCssFilter\u003e.\n\nThen: display_list emits a PRIM_BACKDROP record after a node's outer shadows and before its fill, with the box's bounds, radii, corner shape, transform and clips; color.r the blur deviation in pixels, color.g three deviations in layout units for the row pass's growth; the colour matrix in color2, border, borderColor (filter_matrix). Props BackdropBlur and colour amounts like the filter ones; Tw classes backdrop-blur-xs … 3xl, backdrop-brightness-, -contrast-, -grayscale, -hue-rotate-, -invert, -saturate-, -sepia, -opacity-. Render probe: red and blue halves under a backdrop-blur box show a mix in the middle and stay apart outside it.","files":null}]}